# deploy/poc/versions.env — every version the PoC profile installs, in one place.
# Sourced by the commands in deploy/poc/README.md and by deploy/poc/validate.sh.
# Change a line here and nowhere else; README.md records why each one is pinned.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Logweir
# The release: the chart AND the four images of ONE `main` publication.
# images.yml publishes the images as `sha-<commit>` and, in the same run and
# after them, the chart as `oci://registry-1.docker.io/vladyslavhaina/
# logweir-chart --version 0.1.0-sha-<commit>`, whose image defaults are those
# same four tags (scripts/ci-images.sh `chart`).
#
# THIS PROFILE NEEDS A BUILD THAT CONTAINS THE CHART-GAP FIXES — the console's
# `oidc.caBundleFile` and `trustedProxyService`, the controller's `--probe` —
# which every `main` publication since `claude/chart-poc` (first: `86a554e6`,
# CI run 35957294926) carries. LOGWEIR_COMMIT names main `fdb48cd8` (CI run
# 36183088296, 2026-09-25), the first publication with the fix for the
# defect the PoC round on `815249cb` found (P16: a follow's repaint now
# keeps the reader's place) and the Catalog's code spans (O2); its four
# images and chart were pulled anonymously from Docker Hub before this
# pin, and the running PoC was upgraded to it from `815249cb` (itself
# upgraded from `a54fb823`, from `b748fd5f`, from `02dc44b6` and from
# `86a554e6`) with README.md "Upgrade to a newer publication". A build
# older than `86a554e6` CANNOT stand in for it: its console refuses the
# configuration (exit 2, `unknown field`) and its controller fails the exec
# probes.
#
# A RELEASE PIN (PROD-14.0). Since `v0.2.0-rc.1` the profile pins a RELEASE:
# the tag promotes one `sha-<commit>` publication unchanged, and its chart
# `--version <semver>` names the four images as `:<tag>@sha256:…` (the tag says
# which release, the digest decides which bytes). LOGWEIR_COMMIT is that
# publication (release.json `.images.publication`), LOGWEIR_TAG the release
# tag, and LOGWEIR_IMAGE_DIGESTS the release.json `.images.refs[*].digest`
# values, which validate.sh hands `scripts/ci-images.sh chart-package` as
# IMAGE_DIGESTS (a release chart refuses to package without them). For a
# `sha-` publication set LOGWEIR_TAG=sha-$LOGWEIR_COMMIT,
# LOGWEIR_CHART_VERSION=0.1.0-sha-$LOGWEIR_COMMIT and LOGWEIR_IMAGE_DIGESTS
# empty. The PoC was upgraded in place from `ea9788cf` to `v0.2.0-rc.1` on
# 2026-10-08 (PoC batch 2), and from `v0.2.0-rc.1` to the `sha-` publication of
# main `5127af8a` (CI run 37753000930: PROD-00.3f's engine 0.23.3, PROD-16.1
# with `identity.bootstrapFeatures.consoleKey` on, PROD-08.1, FX-17) on
# 2026-10-08 (PoC batch 3), to main `d41aae06` (PROD-01.3, PROD-05.1, FX-16,
# PROD-00.2's two-platform signed images and engine 0.23.3+logweir.1, FX-20,
# FX-18, FX-24) on 2026-10-09 (PoC batch 4), to main `739f17c5` (FX-21's
# engine 0.23.3+logweir.2, PROD-11.1's window start, PROD-08.1a's complete
# coverage through the CRDs, API and console, FX-24b, FX-29) on 2026-10-09
# (PoC batch 5), and to main `d53da293` (PROD-03.0's schema dependency,
# FX-28, FX-20c, PROD-01.4a's topic ids, PROD-04.1's consumer positions,
# PROD-11.1b's partition subsets, FX-31, FX-24c, FX-19, FX-13a and FX-32) on
# 2026-10-10 (PoC batch 6), and to main `8d121b33` (PROD-15.1's original-name
# restores, FX-14, FX-22, FX-48, PROD-01.2, FX-34, FX-27, FX-42 item 1, FX-35,
# FX-39/40, FX-33 and PROD-16.2's two-person console approval; CI run
# 38111575687) on 2026-10-11 (PoC batch 7). On 2026-10-12 (PROD-14.1) the PoC
# was deleted and installed fresh from the published chart of main `22dc6147`
# (PR #32: the offline-render guard, the version and architecture floors, the
# recovery kit), as docs/install.md describes, and upgraded in place the same
# day to main `96e601f0` (PR #39, release-notes items 87 to 89: a refused
# retention run named on its policy, the visual pass's console fixes, every
# "Check it yourself" working as printed) with README.md "Upgrade to a newer
# publication" (Helm revisions 5 and 6), and then to main `3c2f358c` (PR #41,
# the Helm chart validated and simplified, `kafka.markerTopic` refused by name;
# PR #42, release-notes item 90: a dropped evidence write re-sent) the same way
# (Helm revisions 7 and 8), and on 2026-10-14 to main `4db6e5bb` (PR #47, v2
# theme A: release-notes items 91 to 97) the same way (Helm revisions 9 and 10;
# theme A's combined PoC pass then rolled back to 8 and upgraded again,
# revisions 11 to 17), and the same day to main `cc59922e` (PR #48, theme A's
# fix round, release-notes items 98 to 101: the evidence read grant, held clones
# re-armed after an upgrade, a create that leaves nothing, the rollback steps;
# CI run 38513884587) the same way (Helm revisions 18 and 19; the re-run's
# older-runner row then set `runnerImage` for one revision and back, 20 and 21,
# the release values unchanged at the end), and the same day to main `519ab67c`
# (PR #49: the rebuilt console, PROD-18.1, and v1.1's FX-30, FX-38, FX-36,
# FX-12, FX-45 and FX-46, release-notes items 102 to 108; CI run 38520556726)
# the same way (Helm revisions 22 and 23; the kafkaclusters and restores CRDs
# changed). Revision 24 adds the deep UI pass's throwaway validation users'
# subjects from a values file that is not committed; the same upgrade without
# that file removes them. The same day the PoC was upgraded to main `63bae2b4`
# (PR #54: the deep UI validation's fixes DUI-1 to DUI-31, release-notes items
# 109 to 115; rustls 0.23.46 and engine build 0.23.3+logweir.4, items 116 and
# 117; CI run 38626279037) the same way, with that values file in both steps
# (Helm revisions 25 and 26; no CRD changed), so the validation users stay.
# On 2026-10-15 it was upgraded to main `05ac11e9` (PR #56: the deep UI
# re-check's fixes DUI-22.3, DUI-22.8, DUI-31.6 and DUI-32 to DUI-44, and the
# switchover bundle and admission hardening, release-notes items 118 to 124;
# CI run 38672454513) the same way, with that values file in both steps (Helm
# revisions 27 and 28; no CRD changed), so the validation users and the deep UI
# re-check's objects stay. The same day it was upgraded to main `8490a8d9`
# (PR #57: the re-check round 2's fixes DUI-45 to DUI-48 and follow-ups F1 and
# F2, release-notes items 125 to 127; CI run 38703013353) the same way, with
# that values file in both steps (Helm revisions 29 and 30; no CRD changed), so
# the validation users and the re-check's objects stay. The same day it was
# upgraded to main `f51c92df` (PR #58: the re-check part 6's fixes DUI-50 and
# DUI-49.1 to DUI-49.3, release-notes items 128 and 129; CI run 38739731052)
# the same way, with that values file in both steps (Helm revisions 31 and 32;
# the restores CRD gained `status.integrity.positionsMapping`, applied
# server-side first), so the validation users and the re-check's objects stay.
LOGWEIR_COMMIT=f51c92df073bb08ae86d4a82cba9cad27c132b9c
LOGWEIR_TAG=sha-$LOGWEIR_COMMIT
LOGWEIR_CHART=oci://registry-1.docker.io/vladyslavhaina/logweir-chart
LOGWEIR_CHART_VERSION=0.1.0-sha-$LOGWEIR_COMMIT
LOGWEIR_IMAGE_DIGESTS=''

# --------------------------------------------- upgrade rehearsal baselines
# docs/release-notes.md (the v0.2.0-rc.1 entry) records the two rehearsals run on 2026-09-24 from
# published builds to the PoC's first publication, 86a554e6 (README.md,
# *Upgrade rehearsals*); run again, each upgrades to the release above. Each
# installs with its OWN chart, taken from this repository at that commit
# (`git archive`), and its own values file under rehearsals/.
#   R1: the last version tag. No console image exists at v0.1.5.
R1_REF=v0.1.5
R1_COMMIT=9cc78a35251df7fcb820d92a62e4c327e8f3ad1a
R1_TAG=v0.1.5
#   R2: the last publication before PLAT-15.2/17.2/19.2 (ac00819) — the
#   lab-refresh-8 build; it crosses release-note items 1-13 to 86a554e6, and
#   all twenty to the release above.
R2_REF=f49849db035d01ff968df7472914f57fc6c2e988
R2_COMMIT=f49849db035d01ff968df7472914f57fc6c2e988
R2_TAG=sha-f49849db035d01ff968df7472914f57fc6c2e988

# ------------------------------------------------------ upstream charts
# Pinned by chart version; each chart's images are pinned by digest in its
# values file here (or by the chart itself).
TRAEFIK_REPO=https://traefik.github.io/charts
TRAEFIK_CHART_VERSION=41.6.0         # Traefik v3.7.13
CERT_MANAGER_REPO=https://charts.jetstack.io
CERT_MANAGER_CHART_VERSION=v1.21.2   # cert-manager v1.21.2
DEX_REPO=https://charts.dexidp.io
DEX_CHART_VERSION=0.24.1             # dex v2.44.0

# ------------------------------------------- namespaces, hosts, addresses
# localtest.me and every subdomain resolve to 127.0.0.1 in public DNS;
# docker-desktop publishes Traefik's LoadBalancer Service on the host's
# 127.0.0.1:80/443. DEX_CLUSTER_IP is the fixed ClusterIP dex.values.yaml gives
# Dex's own Service and logweir.values.yaml's `hostAliases` maps dex.localtest.me
# to, so the console's OIDC back-channel never crosses the shared ingress.
# PoC-only: production resolves its IdP through real DNS.
LOGWEIR_NAMESPACE=logweir-system
POC_NAMESPACE=logweir-poc
INGRESS_NAMESPACE=traefik
CERT_MANAGER_NAMESPACE=cert-manager
DEX_NAMESPACE=dex
CONSOLE_HOST=logweir.localtest.me
DEX_HOST=dex.localtest.me
DEX_CLUSTER_IP=10.96.0.81
